title: StorybookIntro
---
Narrator: "Narrator: Gather round pups, I shall recount the tale of our kind and my mother but this once."

Narrator: "In the beginning, when there were several beginnings..."

Narrator: "and the heavens could not differentiate themselves from the sky, the seed of something brilliant took root and remained dormant until that delineation was made."

Narrator: "To discuss each being borne of arcane association would consume years, yet I may say this much." 

Narrator: "For generations, I have heard tales of humans that exist on lands and take to the sea as seals at will or under special circumstances, occupying stormy strands and frozen tundras."

Narrator: "I cannot recall his name, but in my mother's time, a male selkie was tricked into giving 3 wishes when a human caught him in a net. " 

Narrator: Naturally, the wishes not freely given caused the 3 losses: Famine, Death, and Disappearance."

Narrator: "Mother was caught in the chaos. Pods had been disappearing, and she was not spared of this tragedy. " 

Narrator: "When a pup went missing, my mother made it her mission to get to the bottom of the dwindling food and selkie population…"

===
